.TH DUCKNETVIEW 1 "2026-08" "ducknetview" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ducknetview \- terminal network monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ducknetview
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ducknetview
is a terminal user interface for watching a host's network: interfaces and their
throughput, listening sockets, processes, active and recently closed
connections, a log of what changed, and the host's routing configuration.
.PP
On Linux, per-connection throughput, round-trip time and retransmit counts are
read from the kernel's
.B sock_diag
netlink interface \(em the same source
.BR ss (8)
uses. No elevated privileges are required. On other platforms those columns are
hidden rather than shown empty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-once
Print a one-shot text snapshot and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a fuller snapshot as JSON and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " file"
Browse a
.B \-\-json
snapshot instead of the live host.
.B \-
reads standard input, so
.RB ` "ssh host ducknetview --json | ducknetview --from -" '
browses a remote host.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics
Print the host's network state in Prometheus text format and exit, for a
node_exporter textfile directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " n"
Print the
.I n
busiest processes and hosts and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-usage " days"
Print the recorded daily usage for the last
.I days
days.
.B \-\-usage\-all
prints everything recorded.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-baseline
Compare the host's listeners against the saved baseline. Exits
.B 0
when clean,
.B 1
when unexpected listeners are present, and
.B 2
when no baseline has been saved.
.TP
.BI \-\-baseline " file"
Check against a baseline file rather than the per-user one.
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-baseline " file"
Write the current listeners to a portable baseline file and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-events " file"
Append events to a file as JSON lines. The file is rotated at 8 MiB, keeping one
previous generation.
.TP
.BI \-\-on\-alert " command"
Run
.I command
for each alert-level event. It receives the event kind, subject and detail as
arguments, and
.BR DNV_EVENT_KIND ,
.BR DNV_EVENT_LEVEL ,
.BR DNV_EVENT_SUBJECT ,
.BR DNV_EVENT_DETAIL
and
.B DNV_EVENT_AT
in its environment. It is executed directly, never through a shell.
.TP
.BI \-\-tab " name"
Open on a particular tab: overview, interfaces, ports, processes, connections,
events or routes.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B 1\-7
Jump to a tab.
.B ?
shows the full key list, which is authoritative; the bindings below are the ones
worth knowing first.
.TP
.B /
Search. Prefix the query with
.B re:
for a regular expression;
.B \e
switches between filtering rows and highlighting them, and
.BR n / N
jump between matches.
.TP
.B t
Switch the throughput columns between current rate and session total.
.B U
switches between bytes and bits per second.
.TP
.B z
On the Connections tab, show connections that have closed.
.B g
groups them by remote host,
.B i
filters by interface.
.TP
.B b
Save the current listeners as the expected baseline;
.B a
accepts one highlighted listener into it;
.B B
clears it.
.TP
.B w
Add the highlighted connection's remote to the watchlist.
.TP
.B x
Signal the highlighted row's process, confirming with
.BR t / k / h
for TERM, KILL or HUP.
.TP
.B q
Quit (with a confirmation).
.B Ctrl\-C
quits immediately.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/ducknetview/config.json
Settings, the watchlist, the listener baseline and the alert thresholds.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/ducknetview/usage.json
Recorded daily traffic totals.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour entirely.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
when
.B \-\-check\-baseline
finds unexpected listeners, and
.B 2
for a usage or collection error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ss (8),
.BR ip (8),
.BR nethogs (8)
